* docs(signing): record why the trust-material probe stays single-attempt (#93)

RM-070 asked whether trustMaterial's single attempt at Fulcio/Rekor
reachability is a gap or a deliberate design: it's deliberate. IP
§6.3's backoff-and-jitter clause is about slow Sigstore, which is a
different failure mode from Fulcio/Rekor down — the probe already
gets an explicit timeout, is cached per Signer, and retrying it would
trade a caller's fast, correctly-classed, itself-retryable refusal for
absorbing blips on every first Sign(). Left unretried; the spec's
silence on the distinction is a finding, not something this commit
resolves by editing docs/01.

* fix(failure): compare SIG-004's backoff as a spread, not a ratio (#93)

* test(mcp): exercise Classify's ledger fallback and fix lint (#87)

TestClassifyCarriesTheLedgersOwnClassification drives Classify with a
raw, unwrapped *ledger.StoreError - the branch-coverage gate found the
new case in Classify (errors.go) was reached but its condition never
took the true path, since every existing call site already wraps a
ledger error before Classify sees it. This closes that gap directly:
retryable carries across on a dependency outage, a schema refusal
stays not retryable, and the ledger's own narrowing is honoured, never
widened.

